a0m (88\u00a0ft) high seated Buddha statue at its top.", "extract_html": "<p><b>Ethagala</b> is one of seven rocks that overlook the town of Kurunegala, in Sri Lanka. The rock face reaches 316 metres (1,037\u00a0ft) over the town and in its shape resembles a crouching elephant, which explains the rock's name. It houses a temple, the Athugala Viharaya, and an 27\u00a0m (88\u00a0ft) high seated Buddha statue at its top.</p>"}